think The exploration named the crux (a name bound to a content address) and the substrate (mantra/beading.rye's BeadStore). The rung is the naming layer over that store — invent no storage.
think Wrote pond/apps/tablecloth.rye: a bounded Catalog binds a name to the whole digest + bead-index recipe; store_artifact beads content into the shared BeadStore (dedup for free), fetch_artifact reassembles by name with every bead proving itself by digest.
think Added a Brix-facing render_manifest / parse_manifest for the format tablecloth-v1 flat-Bron catalog — the Bron a Brix descriptor evaluates to; round-tripped name, address, length field for field.
think Symlinked the substrate into pond/apps/mantra/beading.rye and pond/apps/parse_int.rye (matching the existing tally_copy.rye and recall_lap1.rye symlink convention) so the imports resolve at build.
obs Built GREEN on the first try. Dedup dividend proven honestly: storing doc_a under two names deposits 0 new beads the second time (beads_deduped == bead_count). Tamper, unknown name, taken name, empty/overlong name, oversized content, and a bad manifest header all refuse.
obs Honored the migrate-on-touch ratchet: replaced the one std.fmt.parseInt site with tally/parse_int.rye's strict parse_int (leading-zero footgun refused by default), lowering the tree's parseInt ratchet 9→8.
obs Additive — beading.rye stays its own GREEN binary; the witness re-runs it. TAME bans clean, width-check clean.
